  "body": "Refs #499 (partial: the focus bug found by the Mac check of #458; the rest of #499 stays open)\nClaim: mac/m2-lead\n\n**Problem.** Simulator (iPhone 18 Pro, iPad Pro 13, iOS 27.0): a new private message does not open on \"Destinataire\", the new-topic sheet not on \"Sujet\": no caret, no keyboard after 8 s.\n\n**Cause.** `messageFields` is `.disabled(!model.canEdit)` and `canEdit` needs `hasRestored`. `.task { await model.start(); focused = firstEmptyField }` sets focus in the same turn as `hasRestored = true`, before the view re-enabled the field: the assignment hits a disabled field and is lost. Not a simulator effect: the login sheet shows its caret on the same simulator.\n\n**Change.** One view. The first focus moves to `.onChange(of: model.canEdit)`, once (`didFocus`), so a later `canEdit` flip (a send) never steals focus. `firstEmptyField` and its rule unchanged. No sleep. The reply composer shares the code path (not driven on a device: it needs a topic, and the check opens none).\n\n**Tests.** Pure rule unchanged; the bug is view timing (disabled state vs focus), only observable on a real focus state, so no unit test. Local XCUITest driver (not committed) reading `hasKeyboardFocus`, 3 s after the sheet appears:\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| iPhone 18 Pro, new MP, Destinataire | focus 0, keyboards 0 | focus 1, keyboards 1 |\n| iPhone 18 Pro, new topic, Sujet | 0 / 0 | 1 / 1 |\n| iPad Pro 13, new MP | 0 / 0 | 1 / 1 |\n| iPad Pro 13, new topic | 0 / 0 | 1 / 1 |\n\nNothing sent; drafts emptied. No CHANGELOG-LEGACY row (the port's intent, not a legacy change).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * The reply composer now waits until the draft is ready and fields are editable before focusing the first empty field. This ensures initial focus is directed to a field that is available for editing, rather than being assigned while fields are disabled.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
